<title>GERMANY: Germany's Grundig sees another loss in 97.</title>
<headline>Germany's Grundig sees another loss in 97.</headline>
<dateline>FUERTH, Germany 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's troubled electronics group Grundig AG, a subsidiary of Philips NV, said on Monday results would improve next year but that the company expected to remain in the red.</p>
<p>&quot;But results will improve considerably,&quot; a Grundig spokesman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>Earlier this month, Grundig predicted its net loss in 1996 would total 250 million marks ($160.9 million).</p>
<p>The spokesman said at the end of the year, Grundig will have a workforce of some 8,500 employees, around 3,000 fewer than the previous year. Another 100 jobs are expected to be cut in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
<p>($ = 1.554 German Marks)</p>
